# Two ways to provide credentials — pick whichever fits your workflow:
#
#  (1) Shell environment variable (preferred):
#        export S2_API_KEY=...
#      The client picks this up automatically. Survives restarts if added to
#      ~/.zshrc / ~/.bashrc, and stays out of version control.
#
#  (2) .env file in this directory (or any parent up to 5 levels):
#        cp .env.example .env
#        # then fill in the value
#      The s2_client auto-loads .env if present. Lower precedence than the
#      shell env var (env var wins if both are set).
#
# The client reads S2_API_KEY first, then falls back to SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY.

S2_API_KEY=your-key-here
